  "finding": "Original evidence attribution only collects artifact IDs from read/grep call arguments. A legitimate cursor read omits id, so the legacy 27B task is falsely marked as not recovering required evidence despite its returned exact page.",
  "correction": "The separate v2 adapter attributes only successful cursor reads to a previously owner-issued cursor and matching returned artifact ID, links that identity through a model-visible compiled preview to the original immutable source hash, verifies the exact returned byte range, and requires the query in those returned bytes. It then applies the unchanged original criterion with that proven identity. Search actions are not reclassified; original retrieval counts, usage, tool calls and other criteria stay unchanged.",
